1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,950
Let's walk back along the high street where you'll come across several important and colleges.
沿 High Street 走回去，会经过字幕说的 several important and colleges，指一些重要地点和学院。

2
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:11,390
The first is the radcliffe camera probably the most photographed building in the city.
第一处是 Radcliffe Camera，可能是城里被拍照最多的建筑。

3
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:17,800
It's a huge circular library used by students you can't go inside unless you're a bodleian card holder.
它是学生用的巨大圆形图书馆，除非持有 Bodleian 读者证，否则进不去。

4
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:20,790
But the exterior is spectacular.
不过外观很壮观。

5
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:27,759
The second is the bodleian library one of the oldest libraries in Europe founded in 1602.
第二处是 Bodleian 图书馆，作者介绍它是欧洲最古老的图书馆之一，创立于一六〇二年。

6
00:00:27,759 --> 00:00:34,350
And in here you can see the divinity school with the stunning medieval vaulted ceiling.
这里能看到 Divinity School 和令人惊艳的中世纪拱顶天花板。

7
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:39,110
This is where you'll get that stereotypical shot of oxford.
在这里可以拍到人们心中那种典型的牛津照片。

8
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:46,710
The duke humfrey's library is used in the harry potter films and the old schools quadrangle is literally picture perfect.
Duke Humfrey's 图书馆曾用于《哈利·波特》电影，Old Schools Quadrangle 简直美得像画。

9
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:52,749
Around here you'll also find the hertford bridge otherwise known as the bridge of sighs.
附近还有 Hertford Bridge，也叫叹息桥。

10
00:00:52,759 --> 00:00:59,040
This is similar to the bridge of sighs in venice and is a picturesque bridge that joins two college buildings together.
它和威尼斯叹息桥相似，是一座连接两栋学院建筑的漂亮桥梁。

11
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:03,430
It's definitely worth a look and it's a nice photo opportunity.
很值得一看，也是拍照的好地方。

12
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:09,910
Oh and if you do get access to all souls college across the street that too is spectacular.
如果能进入街对面的 All Souls College，那里也非常壮观。

13
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:16,200
Just north of the bodleian library you'll find trinity college with its beautiful lawns and classic architecture.
Bodleian 图书馆往北一点是 Trinity College，有漂亮的草坪和古典建筑。

14
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:23,670
And martyrs memorial which is this victorian gothic landmark in the middle of the street.
还有 Martyrs Memorial，就是街道中间这座维多利亚哥特式地标。

15
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:32,390
From here walk north along parks road where you'll eventually get to the oxford museum of natural history and the pitt rivers museum.
从这里沿 Parks Road 往北走，就到牛津自然历史博物馆和 Pitt Rivers 博物馆。

16
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:37,590
Two amazing and completely free museums that share the same building.
两家很棒、完全免费的博物馆，共用同一栋建筑。

17
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:46,160
The museum of natural history like most natural history museums featured dinosaurs fossils gemstones and dead animals.
自然历史博物馆和大多数同类馆一样，展有恐龙、化石、宝石和动物标本。

18
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:50,400
All encased in victorian architecture and a giant iron and glass roof.
这些都置于维多利亚式建筑里，上方有巨大的铁与玻璃屋顶。

19
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:56,630
It's perfect for kids families or anyone who loves natural science.
作者觉得这里适合孩子、家庭，以及所有喜爱自然科学的人。

20
00:01:56,640 --> 00:02:02,510
The pitt rivers museum next door however is one of the strangest museums here in England.
不过，隔壁的 Pitt Rivers 博物馆是作者认为英格兰最奇特的博物馆之一。

21
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:10,160
It's dark it's atmospheric and packed floor to ceiling with tribal artifacts weird shrunken heads.
里面昏暗、有氛围，从地板到天花板塞满了部落文物，以及作者称古怪的缩头。

22
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:19,390
Psychopathic looking masks ancient weapons that are actually illegal to own and random charms and curiosities from around the world.
还有作者形容很吓人的面具、他说不许私人拥有的古代武器，以及来自世界各地的护符和奇物。

23
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:27,150
You could get lost in here for hours but please don't do that otherwise you might end up in here permanently.
你可以在里面迷失几个小时，不过别真的那样，不然可能永远留在这里。

24
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:37,270
If you're not all museumed out at this point highly recommend walking southwest to the most famous museum in the entire city the ashmolean museum.
如果还没看腻博物馆，我很推荐往西南走，去作者所称全城最有名的 Ashmolean 博物馆。

25
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:44,990
This is actually britain's oldest public museum that's free to enter and world class in its collections.
作者介绍，这是英国最古老的公共博物馆，免费开放，馆藏是一流水平。

26
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:53,360
Inside you'll find egyptian mummies greek and roman sculptures asian art paintings by j m w turner.
里面有埃及木乃伊、希腊罗马雕塑、亚洲艺术和 J. M. W. Turner 的画。

27
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:59,040
I like those famous antiquities from all over the world and musical instruments.
那些画我喜欢。还有来自世界各地的著名古物和乐器。

28
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:02,710
Which includes the most valuable instruments in the world.
其中有作者所称世界上最贵重的乐器。

29
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:08,516
It's called the messiah and it's a violin made by the legendary italian violin maker antonio stradivarius.
它叫 Messiah，是传奇意大利制琴师 Antonio Stradivarius 制作的小提琴。

30
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:12,669
It's worth over 20 million.
作者说，它价值超过两千万。
